			"Message": "docs(Grove): Remove deprecated API and proto references from architecture docs\n\nThe VS Code API surface (`Source/API/`), shared utilities (`Source/Common/`), services layer, and Grove-specific proto definitions (`Proto/Grove.proto`) have been removed from the codebase. Update the architecture documentation across Architecture.md, DeepDive.md, and README.md to reflect the streamlined crate structure.\n\nRemove references to:\n- `Source/API/VSCode.rs`, `Source/API/Types.rs`, `Source/API/vscode.rs`, `Source/API/types.rs`\n- `Source/Common/Traits.rs`, `Source/Common/Error.rs`\n- `Source/Services/` directory\n- `Proto/Grove.proto` — Grove now uses `Vine.proto` for gRPC communication with Mountain\n\nUpdate the sequence diagram to specify \"gRPC via Vine\" instead of \"Grove.proto\". Adjust the principle table in README.md to remove the API Compatibility row and simplify the Composability description to focus on host and transport separation.\n\nThis ensures the documentation accurately represents the current Grove architecture where the API layer has been integrated directly into the Host and Transport components, and protocol definitions are inherited from the Vine contract.",
